Issue #1407 -- chat and console 502s. Measurement, root cause, and A/B proof.
Captured 2026-08-29 against the demo box (ssh hive-demo), which was serving
commit 7e68b645e04ab57ffb0898166b8d4ff14bc9ee13 at the start of the session.
No credential appears in any URL below, so nothing required redaction.

================================================================================
1. RE-MEASUREMENT (the issue's counts were right, its attribution was not)
================================================================================

$ docker logs --since 24h hive-caddy-owui-1 2>&1 | grep -c '"status":502'
55

$ docker logs --since 24h hive-caddy-owui-1 2>&1 \
    | grep -o 'lookup [a-z-]* on 127.0.0.11:53: [a-z ]*' | sort | uniq -c
     17 lookup open-webui on 127.0.0.11:53: server misbehaving

$ docker logs --since 24h hive-caddy-owui-1 2>&1 | grep -c 'connect: connection refused'
38

Other origins over the same window:
  hive-caddy-console-1    502s=3
  hive-caddy-supabase-1   502s=0
  hive-caddy-artifacts-1  502s=0

================================================================================
2. THE 502s ARE NOT SPREAD OUT. THEY ARE NINE DEPLOY WINDOWS.
================================================================================

$ docker logs --since 24h -t hive-caddy-owui-1 2>&1 | grep '"status":502' \
    | awk '{print $1}' | cut -c1-19 | sort

  burst                    duration   deploy run covering it
  20:39:28 -> 20:40:08       40s      yes
  21:24:21 -> 21:24:58       37s      yes
  22:11:40 -> 22:11:48        8s      yes
  22:35:46 -> 22:35:58       12s      yes
  02:33:11 -> 02:33:23       12s      yes
  02:49:33                 single     yes
  08:05:11                 single     33242252839, 08:03:27Z -> 08:07:27Z
  09:33:02 -> 09:33:31       29s      33245684859, 09:31:20Z -> 09:35:35Z
  09:52:57 -> 09:53:01        4s      33246425110, 09:50:35Z -> 09:55:16Z

Zero 502s outside a deploy window. The container serving chat at capture time
confirms the last of those exactly:

$ docker inspect hive-open-webui-1 --format 'created={{.Created}} started={{.State.StartedAt}}'
created=2026-08-29T09:52:55.347821652Z started=2026-08-29T09:53:10.893215947Z

The 09:52:57 -> 09:53:01 burst sits between those two timestamps.

================================================================================
3. MECHANISM: THE EMBEDDED RESOLVER SERVFAILS A NAME IT NO LONGER HOLDS
================================================================================

$ docker exec hive-caddy-owui-1 cat /etc/resolv.conf
nameserver 127.0.0.11
search .
options edns0 trust-ad ndots:0
# Based on host file: '/etc/resolv.conf' (internal resolver)
# ExtServers: [host(127.0.0.53)]

$ docker exec hive-caddy-owui-1 nslookup -type=a open-webui 127.0.0.11
Name:	open-webui
Address: 172.18.0.19

$ docker exec hive-caddy-owui-1 nslookup -type=a nosuchcontainer 127.0.0.11
** server can't find nosuchcontainer: SERVFAIL

SERVFAIL, not NXDOMAIN: Docker's embedded DNS forwards a name it does not hold
to the host resolver named above (systemd-resolved at 127.0.0.53), which
refuses a single-label name. Go's resolver reports SERVFAIL as "server
misbehaving". So while the old container is gone and the new one has not
registered, the lookup fails; once it has registered but uvicorn is not
listening yet, the dial is refused. Two error strings, one recreate window.

================================================================================
4. A/B ON THE REAL ARTIFACT (red first, then green)
================================================================================

Harness: a throwaway user-defined Docker network, `caddy502test`, holding no
containers, so `open-webui` is exactly the unresolvable single-label name the
recreate window produces. The repo's own Caddyfile.owui is mounted unchanged
into caddy:2-alpine at the digest docker-compose.yml pins.

--- RED: Caddyfile.owui as it stands on main -----------------------------------
$ /tmp/caddy502/ab502.sh pre 18099
--- pre container status ---
Up 3 seconds
--- pre: 5 requests to / ---
code=502 time=0.003772
code=502 time=0.003772
code=502 time=0.003526
code=502 time=0.003418
code=502 time=0.003365
--- pre caddy error log (last 2) ---
"msg":"dial tcp: lookup open-webui on 127.0.0.11:53: server misbehaving"
"msg":"dial tcp: lookup open-webui on 127.0.0.11:53: server misbehaving"

The error string is character-for-character the one production logged.

--- GREEN: same file with lb_try_duration 30s / lb_try_interval 1s -------------
$ /tmp/caddy502/ab502.sh post 18098
--- post container status ---
Up 3 seconds
--- post: 5 requests to / ---
code=502 time=30.095174
code=502 time=30.094721
code=502 time=30.094784
code=502 time=30.093050
code=502 time=30.096884
--- post caddy error log (last 2) ---
"msg":"dial tcp: lookup open-webui on 127.0.0.11:53: server misbehaving"
"msg":"dial tcp: lookup open-webui on 127.0.0.11:53: server misbehaving"

This is the half that matters for the "do not mask a real failure" rule. An
upstream that never comes back still gets a real 502, at the stated bound
(30.09s against a declared 30s) and not a second longer, and the underlying
error is still logged verbatim. Nothing is hidden; the failure is delayed.

--- GREEN: transient outage, which is what a deploy actually is ----------------
The request is issued while the upstream does not exist, and the upstream
container is started while the request is still in flight.

$ /tmp/caddy502/recover502.sh pre 18099
=== pre: upstream absent at request time, appears after 8s ===
code=502 time=0.003064

$ /tmp/caddy502/recover502.sh post 18098
=== post: upstream absent at request time, appears after 8s ===
code=200 time=9.044268

502 in 3ms becomes 200 in 9s. That is the whole defect and the whole fix.

--- NO REGRESSION: patched config against the LIVE chat upstream ---------------
Same patched Caddyfile, this time on the real compose network, fronting the
running hive-open-webui-1 container, bound to loopback only and mounting
nothing the real stack shares:

$ /tmp/caddy502/liveharness.sh
--- live harness status ---
Up 3 seconds
--- real chat upstream through the patched config ---
code=200 time=0.012091

12ms. The retry costs a healthy request nothing, because a retry loop that
never fails never iterates.

--- CONFIG VALIDITY ------------------------------------------------------------
$ docker run --rm -v .../Caddyfile.post:/etc/caddy/Caddyfile:ro caddy:2-alpine \
    caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
Valid configuration

$ (same for the patched Caddyfile.console)
Valid configuration

